# SQL Data Warehouse Project

A hands-on SQL project built on SQL Server 2025, focused on transforming raw sales data into analytics-ready views using a medallion-style architecture (gold layer).

## Overview

This project uses a `DatawarehouseAnalytics` database with a `gold` schema containing fact and dimension tables, plus reporting views built on top of them for customer and product analysis.

### Core Tables
- `gold.fact_sales` — transactional sales data (orders, quantities, sales amounts)
- `gold.dim_customers` — customer details (names, birthdate, customer keys)
- `gold.dim_products` — product details (names, categories, cost)

### Reporting Views
- **`gold.report_customers`** — consolidates customer-level metrics including:
  - Age and age group segmentation
  - Customer segment (VIP / Regular / New) based on spending and lifespan
  - Total orders, total sales, total quantity, total products purchased

  - **`gold.report_products`** — consolidates product-level metrics including:
  - Product performance segment (High-Performer / Mid-Range / Low-Performer)
  - Total orders, total sales, total quantity, total customers
  - Average selling price
  - Recency (months since last sale)
  - Average order revenue and average monthly revenue

## Skills Practiced
- CTEs (Common Table Expressions) and multi-step query chaining
- Window functions (`SUM() OVER`, `AVG() OVER`, `LAG()`)
- `CASE` statements for segmentation logic
- Aggregate functions (`SUM`, `COUNT`, `AVG`, `MAX`, `MIN`)
- Date functions (`DATEDIFF`, `YEAR`, `MONTH`, `GETDATE`)
- Creating and managing schemas and views
- Deriving new measures from dimensions and new dimensions from measures

## Tools Used
- SQL Server 2025 (Developer Edition)
- SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS)
